00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:15.510
One thing you can do
that's really nice in GCP,

00:06:15.510 --> 00:06:17.380
you can actually have
multiple node pools.

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:20.430
So this is the 1.10.5 cluster.

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:21.469
I have 13 nodes here.

00:06:21.469 --> 00:06:23.010
But I actually have
those nodes split

00:06:23.010 --> 00:06:25.314
between two
different node pools.

00:06:25.314 --> 00:06:26.730
Now, the reason
why I'm doing this

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:30.270
is I'm using the first general
pool for my web apps, my batch

00:06:30.270 --> 00:06:32.760
jobs, long-running services.

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:35.687
But this other node pool,
I'm a big fan of Envoy.

00:06:35.687 --> 00:06:37.520
So you've been hearing
a lot about it Istio.

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:40.290
But underneath Istio there's
this nice reverse proxy

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:41.179
called Envoy.

00:06:41.179 --> 00:06:42.720
And Envoy, if you
can think about it,

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:44.136
is like a cloud
native replacement

00:06:44.136 --> 00:06:45.792
for Nginx or HAProxy.

00:06:45.792 --> 00:06:47.250
It has all these
things that I need

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:50.370
to do things like rate limiting
and timeouts and retries.

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:53.970
But I like to actually run
Envoy as my edge load balancer,

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:54.820
even in GCP.

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:56.820
It's the same load balancer
I run on my laptops,

00:06:56.820 --> 00:06:58.175
so I want some parity.

00:06:58.175 --> 00:06:59.550
So what I'm doing
is I'm actually

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:02.070
running each of
my Envoy instances

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:05.310
across these three nodes using
what we call a daemon set.

00:07:05.310 --> 00:07:07.710
And then the last thing I do
to set up my infrastructure?

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:10.950
I create a load balancer that
points to just those three

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:12.040
machines.

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:14.460
So if you think about it,
I have a network appliance

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:16.440
running inside of my cluster--

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:19.610
no extra hops, no IP
tables, straight to Envoy,

00:07:19.610 --> 00:07:21.300
then directly to my apps.

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:22.900
So with the
infrastructure in place,

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:25.014
we can start to think
about deploying our code.

00:07:25.014 --> 00:07:27.180
So let's go back to the
command line really quickly.

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:28.770
So the next thing
I want to do is

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:31.870
