00:07:33.545 --> 00:07:35.670
Every five minutes it's
going to kick that code off

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:37.300
for me automatically.

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:39.390
So my goal is just to
push this cronjob up.

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:42.210
But remember, the price
of admission to Kubernetes

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:43.720
is a container image.

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:45.780
Here's my second trick
that I like to do.

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:49.110
I have this saying, don't
ship build environments.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:50.610
Ship artifacts.

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:53.490
So when I built my
containers, I actually

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:57.690
just build my binaries
locally, upload the artifacts,

00:07:57.690 --> 00:07:59.910
and only have Docker
package it in an image

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:01.920
with the scratch base image.

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:04.740
So my images, roughly,
are about 7 megs.

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:07.510
And then watch how fast the
builds are if I do it this way.

00:08:07.510 --> 00:08:08.926
So the first thing
I'm going to do

00:08:08.926 --> 00:08:11.520
is build that application
locally, take that binary,

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:14.394
push it up to
Google Cloud Build.

00:08:14.394 --> 00:08:16.560
And Cloud Builder's going
to do all the work for me.

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:17.935
You'll notice
